From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:14:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Run QuickJS WPT on pull requests and fail on unexpected
 results

With QuickJS expectations in the tree, the QuickJS WPT run no longer
needs --always-succeed. Pull requests now run it where the Linux WPT job
runs: on the same directories, and on the whole suite when they change
the QuickJS workflow or the servo-quickjs pin. Pull requests that run the
whole Linux suite still only build QuickJS; the nightly run covers them.

As both WPT runs can now be in one workflow run, linux-wpt.yml takes a
`name` for its artifacts and report (default "linux"; "quickjs" here).
`mach update-wpt <run URL>` downloads the QuickJS results too.

Validation: `./mach test-scripts` (pr_jobs: subset, pin bump, pin bump with tests); actionlint on the changed workflows; the workflows themselves run in CI.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also ran the checks above)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .github/workflows/dispatch-workflow.yml |  1 +
 .github/workflows/linux-wpt.yml         | 29 ++++++++------
 .github/workflows/quickjs.yml           | 18 ++++++---
 python/servo/pr_jobs.py                 | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 python/wpt/update.py                    |  7 ++--
 5 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

